ist dismisses the  theory as Superstition and leaves the  family then continued to their final  destination and when Mark asks his  children about the trip so far they  insult the place making fun of the local  black people this and fear viora and she  gets into a verbal argument with Mark  viora feels that Mark enables their  behavior by not disciplining them  however Mark quickly responds that he  will never be like his abusive black  father after a while it suddenly begins  to Reign causing the plane to shudder  violently Mark tries his best to get  them out of the situation but the winds  are so strong that he eventually loses  control and crashes the screen then  blacks out and Mark wakes up later with  bruises all over his body in an  unfamiliar room he takes a look around  and realizes that he is in the Attic of  someone's Farmhouse suddenly the  homeowner Miss Eloise appears and tries  to get him back on the bed but Mark  resists and asks her about his family  Miss Eloise who is very strict and  particular about everything quickly  calls up her husband Earl and their  giant son Lewis the three of them then  try to calm mark down but when he tries  to run away Lewis picks him up and  throws him on the bed like a rag doll  after this Earl informs Mark that his  plane crashed yesterday and that he was  alone expectedly Mark refuses to believe  that and continues to insist on finding  his family he again tries to escape but  just then miss Eloise blows a strange  powder over his face which makes him  fall asleep this implies that the family  is not an ordinary one and they possess  some magical powers either that or  ketamine later miss Eloise is seen  making Mark's voodoo doll which she  refers to as a Boogity doll she explains  that she wants to nurse mark back to  health using this doll after finishing  up she places the Boogity doll by the  window and secures the window with a  white powder to keep the devil away  after she leaves Mark starts looking for  a 